  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Libya, the Libyan General Union of Chambers of Commerce  (LGUCC) is considered an employers&apos; organization. This union is responsible for representing the entire Libyan private sector before international organizations through chambers of commerce and industry. It represents the private sector in most regional and global forums. 

The Libyan General Union of Chambers of Commerce (LGUCC) met by the ILO mission in Tripoli (october 2023), highlighted the priority to change the prevailing &#x2018;dependency culture&#x2019; on public sector employment by promoting formal private sector employment and creating an enabling business environment for diversified job rich, private sector led economic growth. 

The ILO will collaborate with the employers&apos; organization to strengthen its institutional capacity and better serve its members in a crisis setting. This will be complemented by an inclusive, member-driven planning process aimed at developing an action plan that enhances the organization&#x2019;s capacity for directly contribute to peace and stabilisation.</narrative>
  </description>
